  "summary_en": "INTERPOL–UNICRI report summarising the 2018 Singapore meeting on AI and robotics for law enforcement. It maps use cases by development stage, discusses malicious use by criminals, and stresses fairness, accountability, transparency and privacy. It gives recommendations and suggestions for Chiefs of Police, focused on capacity building and international cooperation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AI and robotics are a double-edged sword: useful for policing and exploitable by criminals and terrorists.",
   "Law enforcement use should be fair, accountable, transparent and explainable.",
   "Surveillance expansion requires clarifying legal and ethical boundaries for data collection and privacy.",
   "Recommends sustained international forum, knowledge sharing, pilot projects and awareness training.",
   "Chiefs of Police should build AI units, be smart buyers, and study GDPR implications."
